@en "net/email"
@fa "پست الکترونیک شبکه"
@ar "البرید الإلکتروني للشبکة"
package email

// Entry/index file for net/email - the package's actual code lives in
// the sibling files, all `package email`, auto-included alongside this
// one (same multi-file-package convention as std/archive, std/tls):
//
//   oauth.salam - BuildXOAuth2, shared by SMTP and IMAP AUTH XOAUTH2.
//   smtp.salam  - SMTP client: STARTTLS/implicit-TLS, AUTH LOGIN/
//                 PLAIN/XOAUTH2, MAIL/RCPT/DATA, and a high-level Send().
//   imap.salam  - IMAP client: LOGIN, SELECT, LIST, FETCH - enough to
//                 read an inbox, not a full IMAP implementation (no
//                 IDLE, no SEARCH beyond what FETCH needs).
//   pop3.salam  - POP3 client: USER/PASS, LIST, RETR, DELE - the
//                 simpler fallback protocol.
//
// OAuth is scoped deliberately narrowly: BuildXOAuth2 takes a caller-
// supplied bearer access token and builds the SASL string. A full
// authorization-code/browser OAuth flow has no place in a stdlib
// networking package (there is no browser to redirect to from here) -
// callers get the token from wherever their application already does
// OAuth and hand it to AuthXOAuth2 (SMTP) or Login's XOAUTH2 path
// (IMAP).
